# Open/Closed Principle (OCP)

- Prefer extension points over modifying stable core logic.
- Add new behavior via new strategy/handler/adapter implementations when practical.
- Avoid brittle branching growth in central flows (`if/elif` chains by type/mode).
- Keep interfaces stable and extend around them.

## Review checklist

- Does this change require editing many existing branches?
- Could a pluggable abstraction avoid touching stable code?
- Is new behavior additive rather than invasive?
